INT. STRANDED GONDOLA - ALPINE CABLE LINE - NIGHT

Wind howls. The cabin sways. Frost etches the windows. Five climbers jammed in a space for four. A radio crackles on the dashboard.

ANSELMO RIVERA-FOX (40s, guide, orange parka) clutches the door lever. TILLY HARGREAVES (20s, injured ankle) sits wedged against the wall, face gray. OLEKSANDR "SASHA" BONDAR (50s, beard, ice axe) tries the radio. MAYA KOTHARI (30s, medic bag) kneels at Tilly's ankle. And young BARNABY QUILL (teens, headphones around his neck) holds the cabin's last flare.

                    ANSELMO
          Don't open that door.

                    SASHA
          I'm not touching the door.

                    DISPATCH (V.O.)
          (crackling)
          Gondola Four, this is Valley Control. We have a crew on the way. Estimated ninety minutes.

                    SASHA
          Ninety minutes! She won't last!

                    MAYA
          She'll last. Keep her warm.

                    TILLY
          (through gritted teeth)
          I'm fine.

                    DISPATCH (V.O.)
          Say again, Gondola Four?

                    ANSELMO
          Tell them to hurry!

                    BARNABY
          Can I fire the flare?

                    ANSELMO
          Not yet.

                    SASHA
          Not yet, kid.

                    BARNABY ^
          I can see the lights on the ridge.

                    MAYA
          Sasha, hold her leg while I wrap it.

Sasha drops the radio and grips the ankle with both hands. Tilly cries out. Maya winds the bandage, tight and fast, while Anselmo braces his boots against the sliding door, Barnaby tucks the flare inside his coat to keep it dry, and the cabin lurches another foot into the dark.

                    DISPATCH (V.O.)
          Gondola Four, report.

                    ANSELMO
          (to the radio)
          Four's holding. Seventy-five minutes.

                    MAYA
          (to Tilly, softly)
          Seventy-five minutes. Talk to me about anything.

                    TILLY
          (barely)
          My dog.

                    MAYA
          Tell me about your dog.
